#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192510 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "00b0d838-163d-5299-beaf-255f9b13cf71" :question/math-academy-id "e-11034" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, x^2+y^2 \\geq 4 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A - \\partial A = \\textrm{int}\\, A$\n\nII. $\\textrm{int}\\, A \\cap \\partial A = \\emptyset$\n\nIII. $A = \\textrm{int}\\,A \\cup \\partial A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $\\partial A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $\\partial A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/2c/2c7e7ac1b320591250b045ebe493b28e0bb9cdb38469324ee496aacb8766c75b.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\textrm{int}\\, A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\textrm{int}\\,A = A - \\partial A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/49/49ffc47c2ae1cde5e93e8607db8ef6b58eb7938913f82ea41f281df1fe334c14.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\textrm{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A - \\partial A = \\textrm{int}\\, A.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\textrm{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\textrm{int}\\, A \\cap \\partial A = \\emptyset,$ where $\\emptyset$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points, so we must have $A = \\textrm{int}\\,A \\cup \\partial A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192511 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Interior of a Set"}] :question/id #uuid "a8045dd8-90b8-5671-9003-2539c502cb49" :question/math-academy-id "e-11035" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\,  y^2 - 1 \\leq  x , \\, -2 \\leq y \\leq  2 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{int}\\,A = \\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, \\bbox[5px, border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}, \\, -2 <     y <     2\\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $\\partial A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $\\partial A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/1c/1ca3afd22a68f2ce8b29645879967c3d130d5c19a7d529296ff129eb92693295.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\textrm{int}\\, A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\textrm{int}\\,A = A - \\partial A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/6e/6e7f7a326a89c60bbc11e48d491ed05a176161881368f189aec7aad916752b64.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{int}\\,A = \\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, \\bbox[5px, border: 1px solid black]{y^2 - 1 < x}, \\, -2 <     y <     2\\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192530 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Boundary of a Set"}] :question/id #uuid "44971e25-0367-5b13-a6be-db503c6b4539" :question/math-academy-id "e-12399" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{(x,y) \\in\\mathbb R^2 : x^2+y^2 -1<0\\}\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\partial A = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,: \\bbox[5px, border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}} \\, \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $\\partial A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $\\partial A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/8d/8d3c7549948f0dd0f6a634526f1d978ae69d0c5b25611981b63a7cf389608087.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the circle $x^2+y^2 = 1.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\partial A = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, \\bbox[5px, border: 1px solid black]{x^2+y^2 = 1} \\, \\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Boundary of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14199fda-1604-5471-af77-6b063ea475fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\ge 4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272568} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd770e5-1e9e-5b3b-9114-12a60ab0eecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272813} {:answer/id #uuid "46484d1f-af25-5d4e-b175-bb8a36b72897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}<4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272986} {:answer/id #uuid "57376c97-3e48-5777-a062-5ab68c9ec42b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}>4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273135} {:answer/id #uuid "f25db4dd-094f-5115-9b15-6297c4b48ddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\le 4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fd770e5-1e9e-5b3b-9114-12a60ab0eecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272813} :answer-field/id #uuid "46520efc-6964-5bb8-b02c-6739529e29ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9afd51d6-5b72-58c9-b163-8fcc7c81ce98" :question/math-academy-id "q-158313" :question/problem "![](images/c2/c2452160f8af4651bdc78756b7c0df8402de185ba7a7bedbc1c1a676b342af97.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/eea68ab4e4b440609fcc4f6c2d40c4dc9fc394fc45f1047ec9c658729322749a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=4x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=4x\\,}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Boundary of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaf2fb43-bdc0-5841-a39a-f7cffa6bcb79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{2} + y^{2} = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191117} {:answer/id #uuid "ad93a534-2c98-53bc-9aec-efcb60249af1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{2} + y^{2} > 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191118} {:answer/id #uuid "c1a306d2-7b05-54fc-813e-7084bf885144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{2} + y^{2} \\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191119} {:answer/id #uuid "d9476125-aa4f-506e-8ea7-116c01a04aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{2} + y^{2} < 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191120} {:answer/id #uuid "de89cac3-f89c-5d27-8aea-140f933f0489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{2} + y^{2} \\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191121}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b63982e2-3147-52ee-8732-e0d8c992bc45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191116}] :question/id #uuid "e571fd67-bd94-5783-aad5-ab93b8b67cb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-161440" :question/problem "Consider the set $A$, defined by\n$A = {(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: 4x^{2} + y^{2} > 4}$.\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n$∂A = {(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: A A A A A}$.\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6df4c2be-04e6-571f-b0a9-dfab0dd98141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448466} {:answer/id #uuid "6e49a39a-5368-5de8-8c63-144924ac30d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e49a39a-5368-5de8-8c63-144924ac30d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448467} :answer-field/id #uuid "efee37f6-b4c6-545d-bd91-c2a4f79965cc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449273} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a00d201-d27c-52d0-8af0-2805fae6cd94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448468} {:answer/id #uuid "75d7e2d1-7f56-515b-bd02-787ded8e5270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75d7e2d1-7f56-515b-bd02-787ded8e5270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448469} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2b89ba2-4284-58ef-a934-c6ed5ebe6b7d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449274} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c6ba7f9-51b0-5600-a4ea-f1ca0eedcc9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448470} {:answer/id #uuid "8af85e9b-1a4d-52a0-b5dc-188c47bd77d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8af85e9b-1a4d-52a0-b5dc-188c47bd77d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448471} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4439f51-b7e9-58c6-8132-dce6ead75ac7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "68256c62-7faf-5747-9e8c-b2c67a0a95a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-161444" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n\n- **II.** $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n\n- **III.** $∂A⊂A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/62/62c410c21e79e1bc688c1ff1a3440a207c62bcad42525bdc93fa2770b76d48bd.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/33/33a4738b642443c2535d347aa53ee2b7b80c800142c4844d94578769118ebfbc.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points, so we must have $∂A⊂A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fe507f3-8527-5f21-a721-634b58840b7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459593} {:answer/id #uuid "77761fd6-0e94-53bd-b8c5-72db41020fb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fe507f3-8527-5f21-a721-634b58840b7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459593} :answer-field/id #uuid "06f87cf3-f603-5eff-95ff-c1bae5dbb25b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460663} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2cd58fb-78f4-562a-9420-9f1156d98abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459595} {:answer/id #uuid "12885778-ec5e-53cd-96b2-b72a20448566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12885778-ec5e-53cd-96b2-b72a20448566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459596} :answer-field/id #uuid "08cf2006-06fc-5f94-8e1a-739789d7be8e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "586336b7-1f15-5b0c-a3b2-dad8f88b8daa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459597} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a5df21-20e1-5124-8aa9-f6e537cc7cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8a5df21-20e1-5124-8aa9-f6e537cc7cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459598} :answer-field/id #uuid "882b009d-1a05-565a-aa3f-fa7d9e3e447a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1eb8e242-f7cb-5632-a09c-62dcc98103d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161445" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<1-x\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n\nII. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\nIII. $\\text{int}\\,A=A$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/51/5151df3c5b84ffaca9aa16b401cd9364fea10a240d39c9c28d815b36e417b16d.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Boundary of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "851b80eb-b83a-551c-9279-4549ab4d90e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\ge 2+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378838} {:answer/id #uuid "4f836b32-8260-57b6-b770-2e7d020d9d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>2+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378839} {:answer/id #uuid "13a09149-f988-5eb8-a4cf-60f6541b1dd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378840} {:answer/id #uuid "1b419e90-62ad-5669-bc63-83841ecd51b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<2+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378841} {:answer/id #uuid "0b04c225-061b-5f88-b549-70ae1e62a96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le 2+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13a09149-f988-5eb8-a4cf-60f6541b1dd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378840} :answer-field/id #uuid "40b619c0-07fa-5730-acf5-35ec731f8262" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d973d6dc-e6b7-5c00-a99e-4154f8dbf26a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161588" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le 2+x}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ac/ac2b2f009daf16725be7d3a00743a1d1b75b437b936026fa2be898d94c8c93b4.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=2+x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=2+x\\,}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be55a3c3-a14a-5616-b434-748a64016ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449946} {:answer/id #uuid "9b71986f-ed36-5a4e-9a5f-7dc9b8a49066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b71986f-ed36-5a4e-9a5f-7dc9b8a49066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449947} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0acb8a6-343b-54a7-9d7f-399cf2145053" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450927} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d69f8359-c7e9-5292-948c-328d26d2fcd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449948} {:answer/id #uuid "947dbbdb-26b6-5c81-b11b-1ddb925d5b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d69f8359-c7e9-5292-948c-328d26d2fcd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449948} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a149c98-887c-59d2-92f6-de50cb110a9c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450928} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9b547fe-4e7e-53cd-bca0-9119bfd32cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449950} {:answer/id #uuid "69ad3907-4b5f-5519-bfd6-a21aa64633f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9b547fe-4e7e-53cd-bca0-9119bfd32cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449950} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee22d64e-0f8b-5b04-928a-65a44a0afe68" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4104ec23-658c-58b7-8dbf-72086dab259b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161622" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge -1+x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n- **II.** $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- **III.** $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/3e/3e7d8c11ac4b3de8473741a362ad2b78555c764da2d61f955435e8d59771cf46.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ contains all of its boundary points, we must have $A-∂A⊊A.$ Therefore $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5b39a98-ac20-5cbf-805a-5c64b48f4d91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449958} {:answer/id #uuid "a6123e03-9f1a-55ae-8049-e66f7df48abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6123e03-9f1a-55ae-8049-e66f7df48abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449959} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb5b9ea3-b19f-572e-90a5-93f3f3d18280" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450933} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc09b043-a237-5147-8e74-3cb2d48c0db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449960} {:answer/id #uuid "d3f5341e-9ebd-53a8-b977-c25f8d8c2d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc09b043-a237-5147-8e74-3cb2d48c0db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449960} :answer-field/id #uuid "45b72198-7edb-5c3f-a56e-f84b68b732be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450934} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e755d2a-b5e6-5e96-88fd-d0e6cd0cfc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449962} {:answer/id #uuid "896e016a-452b-53dc-9c84-3690b98756c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "896e016a-452b-53dc-9c84-3690b98756c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449963} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b80112e-c8cb-5761-852a-1dc1da395e6b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "baee2889-195d-5ff5-b660-0a9acac1604c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161626" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n- **II.** $A-\\text{int}\\,A=∂A$\n- **III.** $∂A⊂{R}^{2}-A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/45/4540e03fc5404474a0cd900c89004e6a5cfe7ac2d4702348e9d0395fc1c914e9.png)\n\n \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.  \n\n![](images/2a/2a93b912f0d7b3a84bf0ec9c3b3596d080a9e71a345ff436e2f591edf042d9db.png)\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $A=\\text{int}\\,A$ or, equivalently,  $A-\\text{int}\\,A=∅.$\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points, so we must have $∂A⊂{R}^{2}-A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and  III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3140a798-db1e-5f78-87be-0ad6910ccf12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449970} {:answer/id #uuid "66652cf1-121a-55d6-b60b-7370a097e440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3140a798-db1e-5f78-87be-0ad6910ccf12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449970} :answer-field/id #uuid "0239bed3-bff6-57a4-914e-a2a7696a453b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450939} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51696bef-50a4-5444-9a43-36db6f9afa18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449972} {:answer/id #uuid "42fe6b05-f33a-59cb-bdd4-1fe79fe94856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42fe6b05-f33a-59cb-bdd4-1fe79fe94856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449973} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fcaecef-8c7d-5939-af0c-a44de76b6473" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25836713-0be8-5121-b3d9-e6b2691cc476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449974} {:answer/id #uuid "d419b241-208a-5a0c-b5ad-26a22859c22a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25836713-0be8-5121-b3d9-e6b2691cc476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449974} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f7ad3f5-382d-59a9-a467-493359e62446" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "91207617-bfa9-5efa-a562-b7d640b0c541" :question/math-academy-id "q-161651" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=∂A\\cup \\text{int}A$\n- **II.** $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n- **III.** $∂A⊂A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/a3/a39ecae41a88e873fa9eecb30a5b554be9ec98cf630851715ab35f2f873710f2.png)\n\n   \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/5e/5e473584ef5193b434ff6c138b08c4fbd9111a37252019143b1afb2d48c913c6.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statements I and III are false. Since ${C}_{1}⊂∂A-A,$ we must have that $∂A⊄A$ and also that $A\\ne ∂A\\cup \\text{int}A.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Interior of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21a437c9-898a-560e-9410-f1b54bde1b49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-1\\le y\\le 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278896} {:answer/id #uuid "457a4dac-7b09-53f3-a0b2-fc26b6d17f3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-1\\le y<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279212} {:answer/id #uuid "6b30a6d1-cc0f-5b57-a13e-c4a4b0eff724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279564} {:answer/id #uuid "be011cab-f94a-5242-9219-8918bad94e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280262} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3cde79-af5e-5be0-aee1-d2ce3550f31a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-1<y<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca3cde79-af5e-5be0-aee1-d2ce3550f31a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-1<y<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280365} :answer-field/id #uuid "aec5203e-7431-5285-804f-2b85f96ff86c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45bc0b9a-3391-5849-aa6e-c42fba251f8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161702" :question/problem "![](images/84/84806884f843154c17c338eef0f50d83cae049aece675450e21e58dade6a9f34.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ce/ce268d8b396ea63227734c1edd6b876bb0fe9755fa12a3b75be90c6ef4af5af3.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/84/84780a84406a3fd0e281737b979887e0de6b1e9fe39d440f379fbb2b84e80a3b.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-1<y<0\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Interior of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16ed68dd-7aef-5656-ac3a-0cafe1572795" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\le x<2,\\text{ }0\\le y<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278794} {:answer/id #uuid "38d4ea31-5c92-59e1-b1b8-86206c057d4a" :answer/type {:d